---
title: One gameplay executor and explicit takeover
---
flowchart TD
  accTitle: One campaign operator or one waypoint executor with explicit handoff
  accDescr: The user directs the lead and retains Pause. The lead admits a finite segment and chooses one execution arrangement. A campaign operator sends ordinary commands under a bounded brief. Alternatively, a waypoint planner proposes candidate data and the leased run service executes it. Both reach the same controller and real windowed game. Visible evidence returns to the player and spectator. Lead inspection requires Pause, terminal player tools, quiescence and fresh observation. Role assignment is procedural, not operating-system isolation.
  User["You: objective and boundaries"] --> Lead["Lead: admission, source and lifecycle<br/>Supervision and final verification"]
  Lead --> Choice["Choose one execution arrangement"]
  Choice --> Operator["Campaign operator sub-agent<br/>Ordinary inputs in a finite segment"]
  Choice --> Planner["Waypoint planning sub-agent<br/>Candidate data only"]
  Planner --> Service["Run service and skill<br/>Fresh checks and exact lease"]
  Operator --> Controller["One controller<br/>Native authority and deadlines"]
  Service --> Controller
  Controller --> Game["Real windowed CDDA"]
  Game --> Evidence["Player-visible evidence<br/>Both players use current evidence"]
  Evidence --> Viewer["Spectator: objective and state<br/>Progress, Pause and uncertainty"]
  User -->|"Pause stops new dispatch"| Controller
  Lead --> Handoff["Deliberate takeover<br/>Pause, terminal tools, quiescence<br/>Fresh paused observation"]
  Handoff -->|"New explicit bounded assignment"| Choice
